            <chunk name="Object" index="110">
              <items count="2">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">37d6682d-4b31-4f7f-9bd2-a724ac42403c</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Logic</item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">All urban massing logic in one Rhino 8 C# script (UrbanMassingLogic.cs): street regions from the preset centre lines, blocks (region difference), parks and small green blocks, block overrides, typologies, perimeter/slab/grid footprints, storeys, massing, KPIs and the urban report JSON (output AgentMetric), black edge polylines, display layers and the data for the App Builder UI. The preset street centre lines and their hierarchy classes are internalised next to the script. Street plans (Manhattan, Barcelona, Chicago, Amsterdam) are OpenStreetMap streets fetched with Overpass (see OverpassStreets.gh), simplified to one centre line per named street (straight for the grid cities, curved for the Amsterdam canal ring), rotated to align the grid and internalised in the Preset / Class / Names parameters. The first four curves of each plan are the outer streets in loop order: the site is their closed loop, and the script outputs a name tag plane and text for each (StreetLabelPlanes / StreetLabelTexts, 3D text in the Outputs group, always shown).</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="2">
                    <chunk name="Attributes">
                      <items count="4">
                        <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
                          <X>558</X>
                          <Y>0</Y>
                          <W>420</W>
                          <H>110</H>
                        </item>
                        <item name="MarginLeft" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
