            <chunk name="Object" index="189">
              <items count="2">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">bc9c8715-4334-487f-aad4-01d3b1e781cf</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">App Builder</item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Whole App Builder UI. The App merges four containers, laid out top to bottom in that order:
- Header (top container, purple sub-group): logo, name and Help/Website/Contact markdown links.
- Right container (regular, location right): intro and example prompts text and the hosted agent widget (height calc(100vh - 440px), sized for the 1/4-width right column of the theme).
- Left toolbar "main-toolbar": App Builder has no toolbar component, so each button is two jSwan objects (props: label, icon, tooltip, widgets or tabs; item: id, type, props) and one Construct JSON inserts the list of buttons at .groups[0] of the toolbar object. Widgets and tabs go through Parse JSON before jSwan, and jSwan output through Parse JSON before Construct JSON. Buttons: Scenarios (quick scenario buttons and Reset), Design (icon-only tabs Main, Streets, Typologies, Heights, Display), Key figures (KPI table), Insights (icon-only tabs Floor area, Land use, Storeys) and Blocks (tabs Density FAR chart and Table). Icon-only tabs simply have no name.
- FAR headline: Floating Container at the top right of the viewer (Screen Point + Container Properties, not draggable via the Custom Properties input).
Design tabs and quick scenarios run on data trees: one Parameter Control for all 24 parameters, split per tab by Partition List (D_ParamsPerTab), then one Controls Widget and one Tab component; one line per preset in D_PresetValues, split by Text Split into one branch per preset, then one Parameter Value, Set Parameter Values Action and Action Control. The Block Overrides parameter has no UI control and is used by the agent only.
Data inputs come from the logic script (headline/KPI markdown, chart and table values).</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="2">
                    <chunk name="Attributes">
                      <items count="5">
                        <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
                          <X>2929</X>
