                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Preset street network the district is built on.
Perimeter blocks, slab rows, point grid, or a random mix per block.
Floor area ratio targeted in every block: built floor area / block area.
How much individual building heights deviate from the block average.
Share of developable blocks turned into parks.
Share of buildings with offices on the upper floors (others are residential).
Width of the primary streets.
Width of the secondary streets.
Distance between the block edge and the building line.
Radius used to round the block corners.
Blocks up to this area stay unbuilt open space.
Random seed for the choice of parks and per-block typologies.
Depth of perimeter and slab buildings.
Length of each plot along the street in perimeter blocks.
Distance between parallel slab rows.
Footprint width of each point building.
Gap between neighbouring point buildings.
Lowest number of storeys a building can have.
Highest number of storeys a building can have.
Random seed for the building height variation.
Height of the retail ground floor.
Floor-to-floor height of the upper floors.
Show the block numbers in the viewer.
Colour buildings by use (retail, residential, office).</item>
